#######
# Setup
#######

Context('Numeric');
$initial = 70;
$rate = random(10,15);
$final = random(35,45);
$solution = -($final - $initial)/$rate;
$time = NumberWithUnits("$solution hr");

######
# Body
######

BEGIN_PGML
On a cold snowy day, the temperature in your home is a cozy [`[$initial]\,^{\circ}F\text{,}`] but then you lose power and heating. Your home temperature begins to drop at a rate of [`[$rate]\,\frac{^{\circ}F}{\text{hour}}\text{.}`] How long will it take before your home is [`[$final]\,^{\circ}F\text{?}`]

[_]{$time}{20}

END_PGML

